      "value": "Sorry for my confusing title. I've updated title.\n> Unity Projects already support custom scoped registries.\nYes. Unity already have custom scoped registries in manifest.json of project.\nHowever, AFAIK, according to unity documentation of package manifest, there’s no way to add scoped registry from UPM package. we need add scoped registry manually.\n> How do you imagine \"UPM package manifest to add some attribute to add UPM package registry to project manifest\"?\nWhen I install/update a package via VPM, VPM look for `scopedRegistry` property of package.json and if found, merge `scopedRegistry` of package.json to manifest.json.\nExample 0: if there’s no specified scoped registry\nscopedRegistries of package.json\n```\n  \"scopedRegistries\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"OpenUPM\",\n      \"url\": \"https://package.openupm.com\",\n      \"scopes\": [\n        \"com.anatawa12\"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n```\nscopedRegistries of manifest.json before merge\n```\n  \"scopedRegistries\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": “npm”,\n      \"url\": \"https://registry.npmjs.com\",\n      \"scopes\": [\n        “com.example”\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n```\nscopedRegistries of manifest.json after merge\n```\n  \"scopedRegistries\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": “npm”,\n      \"url\": \"https://registry.npmjs.com\",\n      \"scopes\": [\n        “com.example”\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"OpenUPM\",\n      \"url\": \"https://package.openupm.com\",\n      \"scopes\": [\n        \"com.anatawa12\"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n```\nExample 1: if there’s specified scoped registry but scope is missing\nscopedRegistries of package.json\n```\n  \"scopedRegistries\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"OpenUPM\",\n      \"url\": \"https://package.openupm.com\",\n      \"scopes\": [\n        \"com.anatawa12\"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n```\nscopedRegistries of manifest.json before merge\n```\n  \"scopedRegistries\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"OpenUPM\",\n      \"url\": \"https://package.openupm.com\",\n      \"scopes\": [\n        “com.example”\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n```\nscopedRegistries of manifest.json after merge\n```\n  \"scopedRegistries\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"OpenUPM\",\n      \"url\": \"https://package.openupm.com\",\n      \"scopes\": [\n        “com.example”,\n        \"com.anatawa12\"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n```\n> What does this look like as a feature?\nI want this feature to solve the following problem.\nIf I add some package depends on package on some scoped registry via VPM, Unity will say `An error occurred while resolving packages:` (full message below).\nTo solve this error, package user need to add `scopedRegistry` to manifest.json manually or add scoped registry via GUI. \nError message from Unity:\n```\nAn error occurred while resolving packages:\n  Package com.anatawa12.upm-vpm-test@file:C:\\Users\\anata\\UnityProjects\\UPM-VPM-Test has invalid dependencies or related test packages:\n    com.anatawa12.custom-localization-for-editor-extension (dependency): Package [com.anatawa12.custom-localization-for-editor-extension@0.1.2] cannot be found\nA re-import of the project may be required to fix the issue or a manual modification of C:/Users/anata/UnityProjects/Anatawa12-Avaters/Packages/manifest.json file.\n```",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
