      "value": "@{5e4ca2145f9b3726b3b389e7|full_name}: Thanks for your detailed reply, I understand the feature you want much better now. In short, you want to be able to automatically add a scoped registry to a user's Unity Project Manifest when it is described in a given Package Manifest.\nUnfortunately, Unity's Package Guidelines (published in November 2020) discourage this. I posed some questions around automating the process of adding and updating scoped registries and was never provided a clear answer from Unity - but they're clearly very protective of Scoped Registries and publicly discourage people from using them now. With their sudden change in what users are allowed to do with Packages, we decided that leveraging Scoped Registries was too risky since Unity could pull the plug on them or change how they work or if they are allowed to work at any time.\nhttps://unity3d.com/legal/terms-of-service/software/package-guidelines\nhttps://forum.unity.com/threads/updates-to-our-terms-of-service-and-new-package-guidelines.999940/#post-6687478",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
